============================================================ 1. YOUR
ROLE AND THE GOAL
============================================================

Act as a senior product designer, UX architect, and frontend engineer.
Build a complete, cohesive, responsive website and web-app frontend for
Rehoyah, a Nigerian interior and exterior finishing, products,
furniture, and renovation brand.

Do not produce only a landing-page mockup. Build the entire experience
described below: the public website, shop experience, customer account
screens, quotation and booking flows, staff workspace, and admin control
center. Make all screens feel like one real product, sharing design
tokens, components, navigation patterns, spacing, typography, and
interaction behavior.

This project is intended to become a real business website. Make
thoughtful decisions where details are missing, but do not invent fake
company facts, addresses, phone numbers, certifications, prices,
warranties, client logos, testimonials, staff names, project claims, or
performance statistics. Use clearly labeled editable demo
data/placeholders instead.

The site must look crafted by a thoughtful human design team: elegant,
practical, editorial, confident, and restrained. Avoid generic
AI-generated website aesthetics, excessive gradients, glowing cards,
random blobs, glassmorphism everywhere, overdone animations, meaningless
floating shapes, fake dashboards full of arbitrary charts, oversized
rounded cards on every element, stock-looking illustrations, and
decorative graphics that distract from the real content. Prioritize
strong photography, clear hierarchy, useful whitespace, deliberate
composition, and usability.

