============================================================ 4.
RESPONSIVE AND ACCESSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS
============================================================

Make the website usable on: - Large desktop - Laptop - Tablet - Small
mobile phones

Requirements: - Responsive navigation, with a clear mobile menu. -
Dashboard sidebar becomes an accessible mobile drawer or navigation
pattern. - Tables adapt to narrow screens: use horizontal scrolling only
when appropriate, or convert rows to readable stacked summaries. - Forms
have visible labels, helpful validation, error messages, and success
states. - Keyboard navigation must work. - Buttons and links have focus
states. - Modal focus behavior should be sensible. - Images use
descriptive alt text where meaningful; decorative images use empty
alt. - Color contrast should be sufficient. - Do not rely on color alone
to communicate status. - Respect prefers-reduced-motion. - Prevent
content from overflowing horizontally. - Use semantic headings in a
logical order. - Loading, empty, error, and success states should be
designed for major experiences.

