I will connect the database and backend myself later. Build the frontend
so database integration is straightforward and does not require
rewriting the UI.

Create a services layer containing JavaScript service modules.
Components/pages should call these service functions rather than
directly accessing demo arrays everywhere.

Required service modules: - authService.js - productService.js -
orderService.js - quoteService.js - projectService.js -
contentService.js - staffService.js - uploadService.js -
notificationService.js

Each module should: 1. Have clear, commented function names. 2. Return
predictable data shapes. 3. Contain demo implementations now. 4. Include
clearly marked TODO comments where real backend integration will replace
demo behavior. 5. Avoid mixing backend connection logic into
presentation components. 6. Be easy to switch from demo mode to real
backend mode.

Examples of function names/signatures (adapt as appropriate):
authService: - login(email, password) - logout() - getCurrentUser() -
registerCustomer(data) - requestPasswordReset(email)

productService: - getProducts(filters) - getProductBySlug(slug) -
